module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.Submodule
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.Quasicoherent.BigSiteColimits.AffineDescent

/-!
# Sections of a coproduct of copies of the structure sheaf

A coproduct of copies of the structure sheaf of a ringed site is not computed section by
section: the presheaf which assigns to an object the direct sum of the sections of the
structure sheaf is not a sheaf, because a section of the coproduct may use a different
summand on each member of a covering.  Its sections are therefore *locally* combinations of
the tautological generators, and this file proves exactly that, in the form the
section-level span conditions of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.Quasicoherent.BigSiteColimits.AffineDescent` ask for.

The mechanism is a subsheaf.  On a site with a terminal object, the sections of a sheaf of
modules which are, after restriction along the arrows of some covering sieve, combinations of
the sections over the terminal object form a submodule of the sheaf whose membership
condition is local, hence a `SheafOfModules.Submodule`.  Every morphism out of the universe
lift of the structure sheaf lands in that submodule, because such a morphism is a multiple of
the restriction of a single section; so if the module is a coproduct of copies of the
structure sheaf, the universal property of the coproduct retracts the inclusion of that
submodule, and a submodule whose inclusion has a retraction is everything.  If the module is
merely a quotient of such a coproduct, the same construction makes the inclusion an
epimorphism, and an epimorphism which is also a monomorphism is an isomorphism.

The conclusion is that `SheafOfModules.IsLocallySpannedBySections` is not merely sufficient
for a sheaf of modules to be generated by copies of the structure sheaf, as
`SheafOfModules.isGeneratedBy_of_isLocallySpannedBySections` shows, but equivalent to it; and
likewise for the two conditions which make up a global presentation.  No quasi-compactness and
no cohomology vanishing enter: what the span conditions need from a coproduct is its sections
up to a covering, and that much is formal.

## Main definitions

* `SheafOfModules.globalSectionSieve`: the sieve of arrows along which a section becomes a
  combination of the sections over a terminal object.
* `SheafOfModules.localGlobalSections`: the sections which are locally such combinations, as a
  submodule of a sheaf of modules.
* `SheafOfModules.Submodule.lift`: the factorisation of a morphism whose values lie in a
  submodule.

## Main results

* `SheafOfModules.isLocallySpannedBySections_of_isColimit_cofan`: **a coproduct of copies of
  the universe lift of the structure sheaf is locally spanned by its global sections.**
* `SheafOfModules.isLocallySpannedBySections_of_isGeneratedBy` and
  `SheafOfModules.isGeneratedBy_iff_isLocallySpannedBySections`: the same for a quotient of
  such a coproduct, so that the span condition characterises generation by the structure
  sheaf.
* `SheafOfModules.isGeneratedByUnit_iff_isLocallySpannedBySections` and
  `SheafOfModules.hasGeneratedRelations_iff_hasLocallySpannedRelations`: the two hypotheses of
  `AlgebraicGeometry.FibredSite.hasGlobalPresentation_over_of_isLocallySpannedBySections` are
  equivalent to the two halves of a global presentation.
* `SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation.isLocallySpannedBySections`: a globally presented
  sheaf of modules satisfies the span condition.

## Implementation notes

`SheafOfModules.localGlobalSections` is the sheafification of the subpresheaf of spans of
global sections in the sense of `CategoryTheory.Subfunctor.sheafify`, but it is built by hand
rather than through that construction: the submodule structure has to be produced anyway, and
the locality of its membership condition is one application of the transitivity axiom of a
Grothendieck topology.

Sieve memberships are compared through `SheafOfModules.globalSectionSieve_pullback_iff`, which
records that restricting a section pulls its sieve back, rather than through an equality of
sieves; `CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.superset_covering` only needs the inequalities.

The retraction argument needs no abelian structure, so
`SheafOfModules.isLocallySpannedBySections_of_isColimit_cofan` is stated without
sheafification hypotheses.  The version for a quotient uses that the category of sheaves of
modules is balanced, which is where those hypotheses appear; they are discharged
automatically at the universe in which global presentations are taken, exactly as in
`SheafOfModules.isGeneratedByUnit_of_isLocallySpannedBySections`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 06WN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06WN)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u v r m t

namespace ModuleCat

/-- Every value of `ModuleCat.uliftSelfHom` lies in any submodule containing the element it
is built from: such a value is a multiple of that element.  Stating this over a bare
`A : RingCat`, where the types are syntactically clean, keeps the scalars of the structure
sheaf of a ringed site out of instance search. -/
lemma uliftSelfHom_mem {A : RingCat.{r}} (M : ModuleCat.{max t r} A) (p : Submodule A M)
    {y : M} (hy : y ∈ p) (a : ULift.{t} A) : uliftSelfHom.{r, t} M y a ∈ p :=
  Submodule.smul_mem p a.down hy

end ModuleCat

namespace SheafOfModules

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{r}}

/-- The factorisation of a morphism of sheaves of modules all of whose values lie in a
submodule of the target. -/
noncomputable def Submodule.lift {M N : SheafOfModules.{m} R} (A : N.Submodule) (φ : M ⟶ N)
    (hφ : ∀ (X : Cᵒᵖ) (x : M.val.obj X), φ.val.app X x ∈ A.obj X) :
    M ⟶ A.toSheafOfModules where
  val :=
    { app := fun X ↦ ModuleCat.ofHom
        (LinearMap.codRestrict (A.obj X) (φ.val.app X).hom (hφ X))
      naturality := fun {X Y} f ↦ by
        apply ModuleCat.hom_ext
        ext x
        exact Subtype.ext (PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply φ.val f x) }

/-- `SheafOfModules.Submodule.lift` followed by the inclusion of the submodule is the original
morphism. -/
lemma Submodule.lift_ι {M N : SheafOfModules.{m} R} (A : N.Submodule) (φ : M ⟶ N)
    (hφ : ∀ (X : Cᵒᵖ) (x : M.val.obj X), φ.val.app X x ∈ A.obj X) :
    A.lift φ hφ ≫ A.ι = φ := rfl

/-- A submodule of a sheaf of modules whose inclusion admits a retraction contains every
section. -/
lemma Submodule.mem_of_retraction {N : SheafOfModules.{m} R} (A : N.Submodule)
    (k : N ⟶ A.toSheafOfModules) (hk : k ≫ A.ι = 𝟙 N) (X : Cᵒᵖ) (n : N.val.obj X) :
    n ∈ A.obj X := by
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ : ∃ y : A.obj X, (y : N.val.obj X) = n :=
    ⟨k.val.app X n, CategoryTheory.congr_fun
      (show (k ≫ A.ι).val.app X = (𝟙 N : N ⟶ N).val.app X by rw [hk]) n⟩
  exact hy ▸ y.2

/-- The sieve of arrows along which a section of `N` becomes an `R`-combination of the
sections of `N` over a terminal object `T`.  It is a sieve because restriction carries that
span into that span. -/
def globalSectionSieve {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T) (N : SheafOfModules.{m} R) {X : Cᵒᵖ}
    (n : N.val.obj X) : Sieve X.unop where
  arrows W g := N.val.restrictₛₗ g.op n ∈ N.globalSectionSpan hT W
  downward_closed := @fun W W' g hg a ↦ by
    have key : N.val.restrictₛₗ (a ≫ g).op n =
        N.val.restrictₛₗ a.op (N.val.restrictₛₗ g.op n) := by
      simp only [PresheafOfModules.restrictₛₗ_apply, op_comp]
      exact N.val.map_comp_apply _ _ n
    rw [key]
    exact N.restrict_mem_globalSectionSpan hT a hg

/-- Restricting a section pulls its sieve of global-section combinations back. -/
lemma globalSectionSieve_pullback_iff {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T) (N : SheafOfModules.{m} R)
    {X Y : Cᵒᵖ} (f : X ⟶ Y) (n : N.val.obj X) {W : C} (g : W ⟶ Y.unop) :
    (globalSectionSieve hT N (N.val.restrictₛₗ f n)).arrows g ↔
      ((globalSectionSieve hT N n).pullback f.unop).arrows g :=
  Iff.of_eq (congrArg (· ∈ N.globalSectionSpan hT W) (N.val.map_comp_apply f g.op n).symm)

/-- **The sections which are locally combinations of global sections**, as a submodule of a
sheaf of modules.  Membership is local by the transitivity axiom of the topology: a section
which is, on a covering, locally a combination of global sections is locally one. -/
noncomputable def localGlobalSections {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T) (N : SheafOfModules.{m} R) :
    N.Submodule where
  obj X :=
    { carrier := {n | globalSectionSieve hT N n ∈ J X.unop}
      add_mem' := @fun n n' hn hn' ↦
        J.superset_covering (fun W g hg ↦ by
          change N.val.restrictₛₗ g.op (n + n') ∈ N.globalSectionSpan hT W
          rw [map_add]
          exact add_mem hg.1 hg.2) (J.intersection_covering hn hn')
      zero_mem' :=
        J.superset_covering (fun W g _ ↦ by
          change N.val.restrictₛₗ g.op 0 ∈ N.globalSectionSpan hT W
          rw [map_zero]
          exact zero_mem _) (J.top_mem _)
      smul_mem' := fun a n hn ↦
        J.superset_covering (fun W g hg ↦ by
          change N.val.restrictₛₗ g.op (a • n) ∈ N.globalSectionSpan hT W
          rw [map_smulₛₗ]
          exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ hg) hn }
  map {X Y} f := fun n hn ↦
    J.superset_covering (fun W g hg ↦
      (globalSectionSieve_pullback_iff hT N f n g).2 hg)
      (J.pullback_stable f.unop hn)
  isSheaf := @fun X s hs ↦
    J.transitive hs _ @fun Y f hf ↦
      J.superset_covering (fun W g hg ↦
        (globalSectionSieve_pullback_iff hT N f.op s g).1 hg) hf

/-- Membership in `SheafOfModules.localGlobalSections` is covering of the sieve of
global-section combinations. -/
lemma mem_localGlobalSections_iff {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T) (N : SheafOfModules.{m} R)
    {X : Cᵒᵖ} (n : N.val.obj X) :
    n ∈ (localGlobalSections hT N).obj X ↔ globalSectionSieve hT N n ∈ J X.unop := Iff.rfl

/-- The span of the global sections is contained in the sections which are locally
combinations of global sections. -/
lemma globalSectionSpan_le_localGlobalSections {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T)
    (N : SheafOfModules.{m} R) (X : Cᵒᵖ) :
    N.globalSectionSpan hT X.unop ≤ (localGlobalSections hT N).obj X := fun n hn ↦
  (mem_localGlobalSections_iff hT N n).2
    (J.superset_covering (fun _ g _ ↦ N.restrict_mem_globalSectionSpan hT g hn) (J.top_mem _))

/-- Being locally spanned by global sections says exactly that every section lies in
`SheafOfModules.localGlobalSections`. -/
theorem isLocallySpannedBySections_iff_localGlobalSections {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T)
    (N : SheafOfModules.{m} R) :
    N.IsLocallySpannedBySections hT ↔
      ∀ (V : C) (n : N.val.obj (op V)), n ∈ (localGlobalSections hT N).obj (op V) := by
  refine ⟨fun h V n ↦ ?_, fun h V n ↦ ⟨globalSectionSieve hT N n, h V n, fun {_} _ hg ↦ hg⟩⟩
  obtain ⟨S, hS, hspan⟩ := h V n
  exact (mem_localGlobalSections_iff hT N n).2
    (J.superset_covering (fun _ g hg ↦ hspan g hg) hS)

/-- **A retraction of the inclusion of the locally spanned sections makes every section
locally spanned.**  This is the only way the main results of the file use the universal
property of a coproduct. -/
theorem isLocallySpannedBySections_of_retraction {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T)
    {N : SheafOfModules.{m} R} (k : N ⟶ (localGlobalSections hT N).toSheafOfModules)
    (hk : k ≫ (localGlobalSections hT N).ι = 𝟙 N) : N.IsLocallySpannedBySections hT :=
  (isLocallySpannedBySections_iff_localGlobalSections hT N).2 fun V n ↦
    (localGlobalSections hT N).mem_of_retraction k hk (op V) n

/-- The inclusion of the locally spanned sections being an isomorphism makes every section
locally spanned. -/
theorem isLocallySpannedBySections_of_isIso_ι {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T)
    (N : SheafOfModules.{m} R) [IsIso (localGlobalSections hT N).ι] :
    N.IsLocallySpannedBySections hT :=
  isLocallySpannedBySections_of_retraction hT (inv (localGlobalSections hT N).ι)
    (IsIso.inv_hom_id _)

/-- Every value of the morphism out of the universe lift of the structure sheaf determined by
a section over a terminal object is a multiple of the restriction of that section, hence a
combination of global sections. -/
lemma fromUliftUnit_val_app_mem_globalSectionSpan {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T)
    {N : SheafOfModules.{max t r} R} (x : N.val.obj (op T)) (X : Cᵒᵖ)
    (a : (uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, t} (unit R)).val.obj X) :
    (fromUliftUnit.{u, v, r, t} hT x).val.app X a ∈ N.globalSectionSpan hT X.unop := by
  rw [fromUliftUnit_val_app]
  exact ModuleCat.uliftSelfHom_mem.{r, t} (N.val.obj X) (N.globalSectionSpan hT X.unop)
    (N.overTerminal_mem_globalSectionSpan hT X.unop x) a

/-- Every value of a morphism out of the universe lift of the structure sheaf is a combination
of global sections: such a morphism is a `SheafOfModules.fromUliftUnit`. -/
lemma val_app_mem_globalSectionSpan {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T)
    {N : SheafOfModules.{max t r} R}
    (φ : uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, t} (unit R) ⟶ N) (X : Cᵒᵖ)
    (a : (uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, t} (unit R)).val.obj X) :
    φ.val.app X a ∈ N.globalSectionSpan hT X.unop := by
  have h := fromUliftUnit_val_app_mem_globalSectionSpan.{u, v, r, t} hT
    (φ.val.app (op T) (uliftUnitGen.{u, v, r, t} R (op T))) X a
  rwa [fromUliftUnit_val_app_uliftUnitGen.{u, v, r, t} hT φ] at h

/-- Every morphism out of the universe lift of the structure sheaf factors through the
locally spanned sections of its target. -/
lemma val_app_mem_localGlobalSections {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T)
    {N : SheafOfModules.{max t r} R}
    (φ : uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, t} (unit R) ⟶ N) (X : Cᵒᵖ)
    (a : (uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, t} (unit R)).val.obj X) :
    φ.val.app X a ∈ (localGlobalSections hT N).obj X :=
  globalSectionSpan_le_localGlobalSections hT N X
    (val_app_mem_globalSectionSpan.{u, v, r, t} hT φ X a)

/-- A morphism out of a coproduct of copies of the universe lift of the structure sheaf factors
through the locally spanned sections of its target. -/
private theorem exists_factor_localGlobalSections {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T)
    {I : Type (max t r)} {N P : SheafOfModules.{max t r} R}
    {ι : ∀ _ : I, uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, t} (unit R) ⟶ P}
    (hP : IsColimit (Cofan.mk P ι)) (b : P ⟶ N) :
    ∃ d : P ⟶ (localGlobalSections hT N).toSheafOfModules,
      d ≫ (localGlobalSections hT N).ι = b := by
  refine ⟨Cofan.IsColimit.desc hP fun i ↦ (localGlobalSections hT N).lift (ι i ≫ b)
    (val_app_mem_localGlobalSections.{u, v, r, t} hT (ι i ≫ b)),
    Cofan.IsColimit.hom_ext hP _ _ fun i ↦ ?_⟩
  rw [← Category.assoc, Cofan.IsColimit.fac hP _ i, Submodule.lift_ι]
  rfl

/-- **A coproduct of copies of the universe lift of the structure sheaf is locally spanned by
its global sections.**  Each inclusion of a summand factors through the submodule of locally
spanned sections, so the universal property of the coproduct retracts the inclusion of that
submodule.  No sheafification instance and no quasi-compactness are needed: a section of the
coproduct is a combination of the tautological generators only after restriction along a
covering sieve, and that is what the conclusion asserts. -/
theorem isLocallySpannedBySections_of_isColimit_cofan {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T)
    {I : Type (max t r)} {N : SheafOfModules.{max t r} R}
    {ι : ∀ _ : I, uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, t} (unit R) ⟶ N}
    (hN : IsColimit (Cofan.mk N ι)) : N.IsLocallySpannedBySections hT := by
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := exists_factor_localGlobalSections.{u, v, r, t} hT hN (𝟙 N)
  exact isLocallySpannedBySections_of_retraction hT k hk

/-- **A sheaf of modules generated by copies of the universe lift of the structure sheaf is
locally spanned by its global sections.**  This is the converse of
`SheafOfModules.isGeneratedBy_of_isLocallySpannedBySections`.  The covering morphism factors
through the submodule of locally spanned sections, so the inclusion of that submodule is an
epimorphism; being also a monomorphism, it is an isomorphism. -/
theorem isLocallySpannedBySections_of_isGeneratedBy {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T)
    [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max t r}]
    [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max t r}] {N : SheafOfModules.{max t r} R}
    (h : IsGeneratedBy (uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, t} (unit R)) N) :
    N.IsLocallySpannedBySections hT := by
  obtain ⟨I, P, ι, ⟨hP⟩, b, hb⟩ := h
  obtain ⟨d, hd⟩ := exists_factor_localGlobalSections.{u, v, r, t} hT hP b
  have : Epi (d ≫ (localGlobalSections hT N).ι) := hd ▸ hb
  have : Epi (localGlobalSections hT N).ι := epi_of_epi d _
  have : IsIso (localGlobalSections hT N).ι := isIso_of_mono_of_epi _
  exact isLocallySpannedBySections_of_isIso_ι hT N

/-- **Generation by copies of the structure sheaf is local spanning by global sections.**  The
two implications are `SheafOfModules.isGeneratedBy_of_isLocallySpannedBySections` and
`SheafOfModules.isLocallySpannedBySections_of_isGeneratedBy`. -/
theorem isGeneratedBy_iff_isLocallySpannedBySections {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T)
    [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max t r}]
    [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max t r}] {N : SheafOfModules.{max t r} R}
    [HasCoproduct fun _ : N.val.obj (op T) => uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, t} (unit R)] :
    IsGeneratedBy (uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, t} (unit R)) N ↔
      N.IsLocallySpannedBySections hT :=
  ⟨isLocallySpannedBySections_of_isGeneratedBy.{u, v, r, t} hT,
    isGeneratedBy_of_isLocallySpannedBySections.{u, v, r, t} hT⟩

/-- Lowering a section of the universe lift of a sheaf of modules carries combinations of
global sections to combinations of global sections: lowering is additive, compatible with the
scalars, and carries the sections over a terminal object to the sections over a terminal
object. -/
lemma down_mem_globalSectionSpan_of_mem_uliftForPresentation {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T)
    (M : SheafOfModules.{m} R) (W : C)
    {x : (uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, m, max u v r} M).val.obj (op W)}
    (hx : x ∈ (uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, m, max u v r} M).globalSectionSpan hT W) :
    x.down ∈ M.globalSectionSpan hT W := by
  induction hx using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem y hy =>
    obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ := hy
    exact M.overTerminal_mem_globalSectionSpan hT W z.down
  | zero => exact zero_mem _
  | add y y' _ _ hy hy' => exact add_mem hy hy'
  | smul a y _ hy => exact Submodule.smul_mem _ a hy

/-- If the universe lift of a sheaf of modules is locally spanned by its global sections, then
so is the sheaf of modules itself. -/
theorem isLocallySpannedBySections_of_uliftForPresentation {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T)
    {M : SheafOfModules.{m} R}
    (h : (uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, m, max u v r} M).IsLocallySpannedBySections hT) :
    M.IsLocallySpannedBySections hT := by
  intro V n
  obtain ⟨S, hS, hspan⟩ := h V (ULift.up n)
  exact ⟨S, hS, fun {W} g hg ↦
    down_mem_globalSectionSpan_of_mem_uliftForPresentation hT M W (hspan g hg)⟩

/-- At the universe in which global presentations are taken, generation by copies of the
structure sheaf is local spanning by global sections, with no sheafification hypotheses. -/
private theorem isGeneratedBy_iff_isLocallySpannedBySections_of_max {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T)
    {N : SheafOfModules.{max u v r m} R} :
    IsGeneratedBy (uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, max u v m} (unit R)) N ↔
      N.IsLocallySpannedBySections hT := by
  have : HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max u v r m} :=
    GrothendieckTopology.hasSheafify_addCommGrpCat.{max u v r m, v, u} J
  have : J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max u v r m} :=
    _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.wEqualsLocallyBijective_addCommGrpCat.{max u v r m,
      u, v} J
  exact ⟨isLocallySpannedBySections_of_isGeneratedBy.{u, v, r, max u v m} hT,
    isGeneratedBy_of_isLocallySpannedBySections.{u, v, r, max u v m} hT⟩

/-- **The generators half of a global presentation implies the span condition.**  Together
with `SheafOfModules.isGeneratedByUnit_of_isLocallySpannedBySections` this makes
`SheafOfModules.IsGeneratedByUnit` and `SheafOfModules.IsLocallySpannedBySections`
equivalent. -/
theorem isLocallySpannedBySections_of_isGeneratedByUnit {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T)
    {M : SheafOfModules.{m} R} (h : M.IsGeneratedByUnit) :
    M.IsLocallySpannedBySections hT := by
  exact isLocallySpannedBySections_of_uliftForPresentation hT
    ((isGeneratedBy_iff_isLocallySpannedBySections_of_max.{u, v, r, m} hT).1 h)

/-- **The generators half of a global presentation is the span condition.** -/
theorem isGeneratedByUnit_iff_isLocallySpannedBySections {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T)
    (M : SheafOfModules.{m} R) :
    M.IsGeneratedByUnit ↔ M.IsLocallySpannedBySections hT :=
  ⟨isLocallySpannedBySections_of_isGeneratedByUnit hT,
    isGeneratedByUnit_of_isLocallySpannedBySections hT⟩

/-- **The relations half of a global presentation implies the section-level relations
condition.**  Each kernel of a covering of the universe lift by a coproduct of copies of the
structure sheaf is generated by copies of the structure sheaf, hence locally spanned by its
global sections. -/
theorem hasLocallySpannedRelations_of_hasGeneratedRelations {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T)
    (M : SheafOfModules.{m} R) (h : M.HasGeneratedRelations) :
    M.HasLocallySpannedRelations hT := by
  intro I P ι hP b hb Z k hk hZ
  exact (isGeneratedBy_iff_isLocallySpannedBySections_of_max.{u, v, r, m} hT).1
    (h I P ι hP b hb Z k hk hZ)

/-- **The relations half of a global presentation is the section-level relations
condition.** -/
theorem hasGeneratedRelations_iff_hasLocallySpannedRelations {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T)
    (M : SheafOfModules.{m} R) :
    M.HasGeneratedRelations ↔ M.HasLocallySpannedRelations hT := by
  refine ⟨hasLocallySpannedRelations_of_hasGeneratedRelations hT M, fun h ↦ ?_⟩
  intro I P ι hP b hb Z k hk hZ
  exact (isGeneratedBy_iff_isLocallySpannedBySections_of_max.{u, v, r, m} hT).2
    (h I P ι hP b hb Z k hk hZ)

/-- A globally presented sheaf of modules is locally spanned by its global sections. -/
theorem HasGlobalPresentation.isLocallySpannedBySections {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T)
    {M : SheafOfModules.{m} R} (h : M.HasGlobalPresentation) :
    M.IsLocallySpannedBySections hT :=
  isLocallySpannedBySections_of_isGeneratedByUnit hT h.isGeneratedByUnit

end SheafOfModules

end
